cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ecc-hypercube: Reed–Muller codes on the hypercube"
abstract: >-
  Dependency-free Rust encoding and decoding of Reed–Muller codes on the
  hypercube: the 2013 hypercube majority-logic decoder (Reed's 1954 algorithm)
  with bit-packed voting, recursive soft-decision list decoding, and
  automorphism-ensemble decoding with maximum-likelihood certificates for
  early stopping.
authors:
  - family-names: Bui
    given-names: Tue
    email: bomot113@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/btue113/ECC-HyperCube"
url: "https://tuebui.com/intuitive-information/hamming-hypercube/"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-11-17
keywords:
  - error-correcting codes
  - Reed–Muller codes
  - hypercube
  - majority-logic decoding
  - successive cancellation list decoding
  - automorphism ensemble decoding
  - maximum-likelihood certificate
  - Rust
references:
  - type: software
    title: "ECC-HyperCube (original 2013 C++ implementation)"
    abstract: >-
      The original hypercube-based majority-logic decoder, written while
      visualizing the Hamming (7, 4) code on a 3D cube and generalizing the
      picture to higher-dimensional hypercubes. Kept unchanged as the dated
      record of the original work.
    authors:
      - family-names: Bui
